{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">2023 AMC 10A #7</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2023 AMC 12A #5</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(cheese-ish)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (cheese-ish)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_understand)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (easy to understand) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(⚡_Just_3_min_⚡)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (⚡ Just 3 min ⚡)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical_(Comprehensive_🧠)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical (Comprehensive 🧠)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Janet rolls a standard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided die <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times and keeps a running total of the numbers she rolls. What is the probability that at some point, her running total will equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341847c55f4196f010e10eba9547b9f5ec2315a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{2}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{49}{216}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{25}{108}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{17}{72}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{13}{54}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"430\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Casework)\">Solution 1 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases where the running total will equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: one roll; two rolls; or three rolls:\n</p><p><b>Case 1:</b>\nThe chance of rolling a running total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> in exactly one roll is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 2:</b>\nThe chance of rolling a running total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in exactly two rolls, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a25c234892fb8a7738bc31e5ccee3bf9ad5afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866bae587c36dd84e78699946c2c9c9998a38a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot2=\\frac{1}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 3:</b>\nThe chance of rolling a running total of 3 in exactly three rolls, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e61637ce2d59296380ccb6f26edee8d45c60850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62985907cfe7f4244cca926033093c391e4e549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{216}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Using the rule of sum we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d4920cb4e7fda0e41565963551fb3eb63cd0468b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{216}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{49}{216}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"214\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~walmartbrian ~andyluo ~DRBStudent ~MC_ADe\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because there is only a maximum of 3 rolls we must count (running total = 3 means there can't be a fourth roll counted), we can simply list out all of the probabilities.\n</p><p>If we roll a 1 on the first, the rolls that follow must be 2 or {1,1}, with the following results not mattering. This leaves a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa9092ba0b15f34c0df746f2e5421a9b4bfc114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{7}{216}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"212\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If we roll a 2 on the first, the roll that follows must be 1, resulting in a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b5132888fe39f38f8dd0fcf4590bca7f72b3169f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>If we roll a 3 on the first, the following rolls do not matter, resulting in a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\nAny roll greater than three will result in a running total greater than 3 no matter what, so those cases can be ignored.\nSumming the answers, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44f552d16abbbea02fa4888498b6c5b038f41f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{216} + \\frac{1}{36} + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{7+6+36}{216} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{49}{216}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"323\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Failure.net\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider sequences of 4 integers with each integer between 1 and 6, the number of permutations of 6 numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/4957864295116ea677c600fdd2ea91cb9deaa637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^4=1296$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>The following 4 types of sequences that might generate a running total of the numbers to be equal to 3 (x, y, or z denotes any integer between 1 and 6).\n</p><p>Sequence #1, (1, 1, 1, x): there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible sequences. \n</p><p>Sequence #2, (1, 2, x, y): there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> possible sequences. \n</p><p>Sequence #3, (2, 1, x, y): there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> possible sequences. \n</p><p>Sequence #4, (3, x, y, z): there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94a096b91beea88234ffd24fc45279b43a87480a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^3 = 216$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> possible sequences.\n</p><p>Out of 1296 possible sequences, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/3242de883f75ed55eb4e5fddcff91edb09397199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 36 + 36 + 216 = 294$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" /> sequences that qualify. Hence, the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e2cf9a45db58c6437efadc2d74cfc8180f32c70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$294 / 1296 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{49}{216}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"176\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~sqroot\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28cheese-ish.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(cheese-ish)\">Solution 4 (cheese-ish)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (cheese-ish)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You have to add 1/216 for the case 1-1-1, so it should have denominator 216. Therefore, the answer is B: 49/216\n</p><p>-Supernova77\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Little Fermat\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=HU7yfXpTg9yBLwSA&amp;t=1203\">https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=HU7yfXpTg9yBLwSA&amp;t=1203</a>\n~little-fermat\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=xtdXIlJmV_1ivP3T&amp;t=1507\">https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=xtdXIlJmV_1ivP3T&amp;t=1507</a> \n~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28easy_to_understand.29_by_Power_Solve\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(easy_to_understand)_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution (easy to understand) by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (easy to understand) by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=3p9Ap7UQ376Tfi1W&amp;t=312\">https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=3p9Ap7UQ376Tfi1W&amp;t=312</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_.5B.F0.9F.94.A5Fast_and_Easy.F0.9F.94.A5.5D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FyVQW-1z60w\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FyVQW-1z60w</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span